issed that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly the Silver Ladder and Giardians order books but they do put nods to them in other places. They even refer to Akhenaten as a Seer of the Throne at one point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T22:49:23-07:00","id":1150084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1150074#post1150074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mostly the Silver Ladder and Giardians order books but they do put nods to them in other places. They even refer to Akhenaten as a Seer of the Throne at one point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool! A reread is in order!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T08:33:09-07:00","id":1150362,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Werewolf/Hunter: Baltic Crusades</b> - During the 13th Century, Crusading Knights begin campaigns to Christianize the Pagans of Livonia and Prussia. The old Gods still hold sway in these lands of brooding forests and haunting swamps, But as the Knights encroach, erecting imposing Castles and establishing powerful Holy Orders in their wake the Pagan inhabitants may be forced to embrace the Holy word of Christ or be put to the sword. The Religious upheaval wrecks havoc in the Spirit world and the Uratha, who have grown used to the old ways of the Pagans, find themselves having to respond, but will they do be swept away by the tides of Christendom. With the Crusaders also come elements of the Church who fight enemies other than Pagans, they know the heathen lands play host to all manner of unholy seed, and intend to see it cleansed, but are liable to butt-heads with other hunters, particularly their equally zealous counterparts from the Orthodox Christian domains.</li> <li><b>Inferno: Early Protestant Reformation</b> - After nailing his 95 Theses to a church door in Wittenberg Martin Luther ignited a bloody storm that engulfed Christendom for centuries to come. The Reformation shakes the Church to its foundations as whole nations abandon Catholic doctrine in favour of Luther's teachings. The Holy Bible is translated from Latin to common languages, graft and corruption within the Church is challenged and the printing press is used to spread new ideas across Europe. But the Reformation has a far darker side: the split in the Church creates untold hatred between Christians: Protestants accuse the Pope of being the living Anti-Christ on Earth, the Catholic views the Protestants as heretics in league with the Devil. Indeed, Luther himself claims that the Devil torments him, makes him doubt. Orgies of religious violence become common as Europe is ravaged by peasants wars and persecution as both sides see the hand of Satan behind the other. But maybe it is not all mere paranoia: maybe there is something else, a dark voice in the ear of the Bishop, telling him that if he simply burned enough heretics, the blasphemy will stop, or murmuring to the freshly converted Prince that violently seizing the Church lands (and the riches held within) would be a good way to fill the state coffers.</li> <li><b>Werewolf: French and Indian War </b>- It is the height of the 18th century, the Age of Enlightenment, and yet the Civilised world is in the grip of war. The Great Powers of Europe are at each other's throats, and the conflict has inevitably shifted to their colonies. In the still largely unexplored continent of North America Great Britain and the Kingdom of France vie for the Allegiance of the Native people in a war to gain control of the other nations colonies. The colonists, who increasingly feel separate from their European brothers, are also called-up as militia. The Forsaken, at home among the vast forests, are forced to either take sides or try to remain neutral, especially when the pure tribes, having infiltrated the European armies, seek to use the carnage as cover to wipe out the Forsaken of the New World. Many Uratha find themselves travelling with raiding native war-parties, or defending besieged forts in the wilderness, all the while their comrades, both white and indian, have no idea of their true nature, until the situation becomes dire enough to assume the Gauru form.</li> <li><b>Vampire/Hunter: Prohibition era New York/Chicago</b> - It seemed like a good idea at the time, during the 1920s a combination of pressure from moralistic protestants and social progressives, combined with broad, bi-partisan consensus, results in a nationwide ban on alcohol. Despite the best intentions of the activists, organised crime syndicates in America's major cities gain control over the trade of booze. Communities are made less safe, while powerful gangsters become richer. It is a time of widespread corruption, backroom deals, mob hits and assassinations, crusading public servants and honest vs. crooked cops. But while the average Joe would kill for his next spirit, there are others who are never short of ways to slake their own thirst, and in an environment where social order has given way to omnipresent crime and corruption, find it that much easier to hunt. They mingle among the criminal-ruling class created by the illegal alcohol trade, while preying on the desperate souls who only want a drink of their own. Then there are those who fight back. Those decent citizens who prey on the parasites that stalk the streets of America's still-growing cities. Those who understand that the Al Capone's of the world are not the only ones who need to be &quot;nailed&quot;.</li> </ol><br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T08:29:01-07:00","id":1151331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>the_1990</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1150362#post1150362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Vampire/Hunter: Prohibition era New York/Chicago</b> - It seemed like a good idea at the time, during the 1920s a combination of pressure from moralistic protestants and social progressives, combined with broad, bi-partisan consensus, results in a nationwide ban on alcohol. Despite the best intentions of the activists, organised crime syndicates in America's major cities gain control over the trade of booze. Communities are made less safe, while powerful gangsters become richer. It is a time of widespread corruption, backroom deals, mob hits and assassinations, crusading public servants and honest vs. crooked cops. But while the average Joe would kill for his next spirit, there are others who are never short of ways to slake their own thirst, and in an environment where social order has given way to omnipresent crime and corruption, find it that much easier to hunt. They mingle among the criminal-ruling class created by the illegal alcohol trade, while preying on the desperate souls who only want a drink of their own. Then there are those who fight back. Those decent citizens who prey on the parasites that stalk the streets of America's still-growing cities. Those who understand that the Al Capone's of the world are not the only ones who need to be &quot;nailed&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mix in some Inferno - or at least Lucifuge - with the phrase &quot;a demon in every bottle&quot; turning out not to be a metaphor.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it went for Capone, but there are many in the Mob who a religious to a degree well at odds with their profession - and also weirdly patriotic. They could form unlikely allies for several hunter groups, or even a compact of their own. Not least because vampires would love speakeasies: a ready supply of drunk people who'll be reluctant to even say where they were, let alone that they were attacked.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T03:16:17-07:00","id":1152147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1151331#post1151331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if it went for Capone, but there are many in the Mob who a religious to a degree well at odds with their profession - and also weirdly patriotic. They could form unlikely allies for several hunter groups, or even a compact of their own. Not least because vampires would love speakeasies: a ready supply of drunk people who'll be reluctant to even say where they were, let alone that they were attacked.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a good idea, you could even have a whole new compact of hunters within the Italian mob. Maybe a bunch of grunts who worked for a boss who got assassinated by a Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T13:51:15-07:00","id":1152290,"title":"","content":"Werewolf and Vampire in Soviet-Afghan war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T14:48:22-07:00","id":1152300,"title":"","content":"I don't see Vampire in the Soviet-Afghan War. Demons, however, that I can see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T15:15:26-07:00","id":1152309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1152300#post1152300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see Vampire in the Soviet-Afghan War. Demons, however, that I can see.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like that idea for 80 demon, Every splat needs the 80s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T15:20:30-07:00","id":1152312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1152300#post1152300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see Vampire in the Soviet-Afghan War. Demons, however, that I can see.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Werewolf + Demon has been done before, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T17:26:31-07:00","id":1152338,"title":"","content":"I for one, am startled that no one has suggested the French Revolution. A societal upheaval, heavy on symbolism, that birthed many new ideologies, all through overthrowing a wealthy asshole-ish formerly all powerful ruling class? I can definitely see Nameless Order mages putting their foot down and refusing to allow the Silver Ladder, all the while the Freeholds of France start to realize analogies to their own Durance in the working class beneath the Monarchy. Bonus points for featuring many different political clubs, which could correspond to any of the Nameless Orders that were the only non-Diamond thing mages could belong to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19270-princevertigo","name":"PrinceVertigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19270_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T17:34:42-07:00","id":1152339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceVertigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1152338#post1152338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I for one, am startled that no one has suggested the French Revolution. A societal upheaval, heavy on symbolism, that birthed many new ideologies, all through overthrowing a wealthy asshole-ish formerly all powerful ruling class? I can definitely see Nameless Order mages putting their foot down and refusing to allow the Silver Ladder, all the while the Freeholds of France start to realize analogies to their own Durance in the working class beneath the Monarchy. Bonus points for featuring many different political clubs, which could correspond to any of the Nameless Orders that were the only non-Diamond thing mages could belong to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, French Revolution has been suggested many, many times. So many times it is Vampire/Mummy/Demon era in DE2. When it originally showed up in the DE1 Kickstarter polls, it was a Mage/Mummy era though. Mage/Changeling/Beast would be a very interesting alternative take, especially since all three deal with dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T17:41:59-07:00","id":1152342,"title":"","content":"Hunters would certainly be a factor as they seek out the monsters repressing them under the cover of the aristocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T20:38:34-07:00","id":1152383,"title":"","content":"And Werewolves would be interested in the disruption to power dynamics that overthrowing the old rule would foster. (Would Revolution Spirits s disrupt the local Spirit Courts? At least until they establish a new hierarchy, same as the old one...)<br /> <br /> Honestly, what Game-line doesn't fit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T20:48:09-07:00","id":1152386,"title":"","content":"How about a dark era dealing with the post-war years between WWII and Korean War, when the world thought for a second, &quot;Holy crap maybe I can finally kick my feet up.&quot; Vampires setting up new courts in the ruined nations, werewolves putting the spiritual back together, mages pursuing making a better world, there's a whole gamut to work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T03:24:32-07:00","id":1152448,"title":"","content":"Anyone proposed the British &quot;colonization&quot; or India, or anywhere during the invasion(s) of Genghis Khan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T06:56:00-07:00","id":1153148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1152309#post1152309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like that idea for 80 demon, Every splat needs the 80s.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we clearly need an all 80s Dark Eras book (Totally Dark Eras?), with each line getting a different aspect of the decade. Demon doing the last parts of the Cold War (everything from The Day After and Red Dawn to the big thawing of relations that ended up giving us stuff like Red Heat), Werewolf covering South Africa in the last decade of Apartheid, Changeling doing the likes of Less Than Zero, Bright Lights Big City and Light of Day, some sort of Innocents thing doing the &quot;horror invades suburbia&quot; genre of Fright Night, Monster Squad and so forth, a Slasher bit about the original zenith of that genre, Promethean in the early 80s Rust Belt, 80s Japanese Vampire, Geist in 80s Britain with an early Clive Barker vein, and maybe New Wave Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T07:04:59-07:00","id":1153154,"title":"","content":"Agreed, an 80s splatbook is certainly something worth looking into. Is there any way to convince the lunatics running this particular asylum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T08:14:34-07:00","id":1153177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1152448#post1152448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> anywhere during the invasion(s) of Genghis Khan?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have mentioned Mongol Empire in general before, not sure if it was this thread though. Werewolf/Geist were my picks for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T11:22:39-07:00","id":1153231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1153177#post1153177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have mentioned Mongol Empire in general before, not sure if it was this thread though. Werewolf/Geist were my picks for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could also see Vampire (for the impending horde threatening their once safe hunting grounds), Promethean (for the wide ranging scope), or Beast (for the persistent fear of being invaded).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T14:37:27-07:00","id":1153286,"title":"","content":"There's actually an interesting potential Demon angle in the Mongol invasions of eastern Europe, I think. After they entered what is now Poland and crushed a force of, IIRC, Knights Templar, the horde had to turn around and go back to central Asia, as the Khan had just died and their leader needed to go try to make his claim to be the next Khan. Had this death not occurred when it did, odds are the Mongols would have continued into the Holy Roman Empire, France and/or Italy, derailing the Renaissance and the Age of Exploration (save whatever the English and Swedes ended up doing).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T08:52:14-07:00","id":1153489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1153154#post1153154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed, an 80s splatbook is certainly something worth looking into. Is there any way to convince the lunatics running this particular asylum?</div> </div> </div> </div>We had New Wave Vampire. I don't think the idea is too outlandish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T12:05:32-07:00","id":1154793,"title":"","content":"I know the idea of 70s/80s Satanic Cult panic as a Beast setting has been thrown around. It would also fit with Totally 80s Dark Eras. <br /> <br /> I unfortunately don't know enough about Mummy to suggest an 80s setting for it. <br /> <br /> Hmm. Valley Girl Princess?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T12:13:23-07:00","id":1154796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1154793#post1154793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I unfortunately don't know enough about Mummy to suggest an 80s setting for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go with Reganomics and the War on Drugs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T12:33:29-07:00","id":1154801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1154796#post1154796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go with Reganomics and the War on Drugs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Relics for the Judges will surely lead to prosperity trickling down?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T21:57:31-07:00","id":1154983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1154793#post1154793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the idea of 70s/80s Satanic Cult panic as a Beast setting has been thrown around. It would also fit with Totally 80s Dark Eras.<br /> <br /> I unfortunately don't know enough about Mummy to suggest an 80s setting for it.<br /> <br /> Hmm. Valley Girl Princess?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Princess during the tail end of the Soviet Union might be more appropriate. Princess is all about political activism, and Nobility would have been right there as the Berlin Wall fell, either for or against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T09:49:48-07:00","id":1155098,"title":"","content":"I'd really like to see Genius set in Europe between WW1 and WW2. One of Genius' themes is how human intellectualism can go horribly wrong, and the interwar period has that in spades.<br /> <br /> You have the very idea of &quot;the war to end all wars&quot; that caused a generation to go to war and die. You have the declining ideals of empire. And young powerful ideas, fascism and communism, promise a shineing new future born in blood.<br /> <br /> Players will be brilliant people, scarred by WW1 (weather they fought in the front lines or not) who realised the ideals they fought for were hollow and flawed and must struggle to accept this. Some will find closure, and others, they will learn nothing and they will burn the world with the light of their Inspiration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1154983#post1154983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Princess during the tail end of the Soviet Union might be more appropriate. Princess is all about political activism, and Nobility would have been right there as the Berlin Wall fell, either for or against.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know enough about East German history to comment on the fall of the Berlin Wall but Valley Girl Princess could work too. Maybe it's not enough for an entire Dark Era but the players playing Princesses reincarnated as Valley Girls and discovering there's more to life through having wildly different personalities in their two forms could be cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 11-02-2017, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T10:07:19-07:00","id":1155106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1154793#post1154793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the idea of 70s/80s Satanic Cult panic as a Beast setting has been thrown around. It would also fit with Totally 80s Dark Eras.<br /> <br /> I unfortunately don't know enough about Mummy to suggest an 80s setting for it.<br /> <br /> Hmm. Valley Girl Princess?</div> </div> </div> </div>Satanic Panic was more of an 80s/90s thing, but the foundation for it was laid in the 70s so...<br /> <br /> Also I would vote the final days of the Soviet Union (including the Soviet Afghan war for Mummy), since the end of an empire would be thematically appropriate for the game-line","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T10:39:31-07:00","id":1155123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1154796#post1154796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go with Reganomics and the War on Drugs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy Vice? I guess the high concept would be Crocket and Tubbs vs Scarface as seen through the lens of M:tC?<br /> <br /> <br /> It occurs to me that Miami Vice debuted in 1984, and that, in addition to the obvious Orwell connection, a lot of pop culture and political stuff from that year would seem to make it an ideal year for just about every CoD game line in some way or another. Besides Miami Vice, it's the same year of the V miniseries, the debut of Highway to Heaven, Lifestyles of the Rich &amp; the Famous, Tales from the Darkside, The Cosby Show, and Night Court, along with continuing series like Cagney &amp; Lacey, Hill Street Blues, The A-Team, Magnum PI, Knight Rider, Cheers, Dallas, Falcon Crest and Dynasty.<br /> Film wise, it's the year of Ghostbusters, A Nightmare on Elm Street, The Terminator, Streets of Fire, Sixteen Candles, Purple Rain, Night of the Comet, Moscow on the Hudson, The Never-ending Story, The Karate Kid, The Last Starfighter, Gremlins, Friday the 13th: The Final Chapter (pt 4), Footloose, Firestarter, Children of the Corn, The Adventures of Buckaroo Banzai, Beverly Hills Cop, Breakin', CHUD, The Company of Wolves, Red Dawn, Indiana Jones &amp; The Temple of Doom, Dune, Dreamscape, The Natural, Once Upon a Time in America, Repo Man, and 1984.<br /> In the world of books, it's the year of William Gibson's Neuromancer, Stephen King's The Talisman (with Peter Straub) and Thinner (as Richard Bachman), John Updike's The Witches of Eastwick, Bob Shea &amp; Robert Willson's Illuminatus trilogy, the first of Clive Barker's Books of Blood collections, and Tom Clancy's The Hunt for Red October. Comics-wise, it's the year Alan Moore started writing Swamp Thing.<br /> Elsewhere, there's the US presidential election (including the first major party ticket to include a woman), the Summer Olympics in LA and the Winter Olympics in Sarajevo, the breakup of the US Bell telephone monopoly, UK coal miner strikes, the Brighton Hotel bombing,and the agreement to eventually turn Hong Kong over the China.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 11-02-2017, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T10:41:10-07:00","id":1155126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1155098#post1155098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd really like to see Genius set in Europe between WW1 and WW2. One of Genius' themes is how human intellectualism can go horribly wrong, and the interwar period has that in spades.<br /> <br /> You have the very idea of &quot;the war to end all wars&quot; that caused a generation to go to war and die. You have the declining ideals of empire. And young powerful ideas, fascism and communism, promise a shineing new future born in blood.<br /> <br /> Players will be brilliant people, scarred by WW1 (weather they fought in the front lines or not) who realised the ideals they fought for were hollow and flawed and must struggle to accept this. Some will find closure, and others, they will learn nothing and they will burn the world with the light of their Inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the inter-war period will have been kind of the biggest blow that the Peerage suffers in 2E. The Lemurian/Peerage conflict seriously flared up around WWI, and when everything settled, people were pretty disillusioned with the whole deal after seeing the carnage. Well, most of them were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T11:51:37-07:00","id":1155153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1155123#post1155123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mummy Vice? I guess the high concept would be Crocket and Tubbs vs Scarface as seen through the lens of M:tC?<br /> <br /> <br /> It occurs to me that Miami Vice debuted in 1984, and that, in addition to the obvious Orwell connection, a lot of pop culture and political stuff from that year would seem to make it an ideal year for just about every CoD game line in some way or another. Besides Miami Vice, it's the same year of the V miniseries, the debut of Highway to Heaven, Lifestyles of the Rich &amp; the Famous, Tales from the Darkside, The Cosby Show, and Night Court, along with continuing series like Cagney &amp; Lacey, Hill Street Blues, The A-Team, Magnum PI, Knight Rider, Cheers, Dallas, Falcon Crest and Dynasty.<br /> Film wise, it's the year of Ghostbusters, A Nightmare on Elm Street, The Terminator, Streets of Fire, Sixteen Candles, Purple Rain, Night of the Comet, Moscow on the Hudson, The Never-ending Story, The Karate Kid, The Last Starfighter, Gremlins, Friday the 13th: The Final Chapter (pt 4), Footloose, Firestarter, Children of the Corn, The Adventures of Buckaroo Banzai, Beverly Hills Cop, Breakin', CHUD, The Company of Wolves, Red Dawn, Indiana Jones &amp; The Temple of Doom, Dune, Dreamscape, The Natural, Once Upon a Time in America, Repo Man, and 1984.<br /> In the world of books, it's the year of William Gibson's Neuromancer, Stephen King's The Talisman (with Peter Straub) and Thinner (as Richard Bachman), John Updike's The Witches of Eastwick, Bob Shea &amp; Robert Willson's Illuminatus trilogy, the first of Clive Barker's Books of Blood collections, and Tom Clancy's The Hunt for Red October. Comics-wise, it's the year Alan Moore started writing Swamp Thing.<br /> Elsewhere, there's the US presidential election (including the first major party ticket to include a woman), the Summer Olympics in LA and the Winter Olympics in Sarajevo, the breakup of the US Bell telephone monopoly, UK coal miner strikes, the Brighton Hotel bombing,and the agreement to eventually turn Hong Kong over the China.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I see it like this<br /> <br /> Vampire = already been done with new wave requiem<br /> <br /> Werewolf/Geist = Miami Vice/war on drugs<br /> <br /> Mage = early cyberpunk<br /> <br /> Hunter = golden age of slashers<br /> <br /> changeling = Last decade of apartheid<br /> <br /> Mummy = Soviet Afghan War<br /> <br /> Beast= Satanic Panic<br /> <br /> Demon = Year of the Spy/1984<br /> <br /> Deviant = ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T15:22:58-07:00","id":1155561,"title":"","content":"Hmm.<br /> <br /> <b>1984: Cocaine Cowboys </b>(Miami and the drug wars)<br /> <b>1984: Hell is for Children</b> (Satanic Panic)<br /> <b>1984: Blood of the Land </b>(South Africa)<br /> <b>1984: City of Ruins</b> (Beirut)<br /> <b>1984: All Teenagers Must Die</b> (Slashers)<br /> <b>1984: Concrete &amp; Crome</b> (LA proto-cyberpunk)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T16:27:04-07:00","id":1155575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1155561#post1155561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.<br /> <br /> <b>1984: Cocaine Cowboys </b>(Miami and the drug wars)<br /> <b>1984: Hell is for Children</b> (Satanic Panic)<br /> <b>1984: Blood of the Land </b>(South Africa)<br /> <b>1984: City of Ruins</b> (Beirut)<br /> <b>1984: All Teenagers Must Die</b> (Slashers)<br /> <b>1984: Concrete &amp; Crome</b> (LA proto-cyberpunk)<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I love those titles. I was going to call the satanic panic era &quot;Read Me Backwards&quot; but your title is much better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T10:12:06-07:00","id":1155767,"title":"","content":"So if the Satanic Panic era were to happen, would we get rules for playing D&amp;D within ChroD? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T11:24:49-07:00","id":1155802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1155767#post1155767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if the Satanic Panic era were to happen, would we get rules for playing D&amp;D within ChroD? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Be sure to check out the <a href=\"http://www.rpgstudies.net/stackpole/pulling_report.html#Played\" target=\"_blank\">Pulling Report</a> for a taste of how the anti-rpg part of the panic went. Patricia Pulling is a good example of the phony occult crimes investigators that offered their services to prosecutors in various trials related to the panic, in addition to her anti-rpg hysteria. Said phony occult investigators would be a great role for a Hero.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 11-04-2017, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T12:59:27-07:00","id":1155827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1155575#post1155575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love those titles. I was going to call the satanic panic era &quot;Read Me Backwards&quot; but your title is much better.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Pat Benatar song off her 1980 album Crimes of Passion, and one of the few top 40 songs dealing with the subject of child abuse, so it fits in two ways. <br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of something suitable for Japan during that year, with the PM Nakasone Era economic bubble, maybe at the intersection between business, politics and organized crime. That or the rebellious aspects of youth culture during the period. <br /> <br /> Also something for Britain in that year. maybe against the backdrop of the miners' strike, compounded by the various industrial accidents (Abbeystead, Oxford Circus, the numerous railways accidents) and terrorist bombings (Heathrow, Brighton) and the long running investigations into police corruption. For some reason it seems to scream for a Promethean angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T13:48:05-07:00","id":1155844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1155827#post1155827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a Pat Benatar song off her 1980 album Crimes of Passion, and one of the few top 40 songs dealing with the subject of child abuse, so it fits in two ways.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of something suitable for Japan during that year, with the PM Nakasone Era economic bubble, maybe at the intersection between business, politics and organized crime. That or the rebellious aspects of youth culture during the period.<br /> <br /> Also something for Britain in that year. maybe against the backdrop of the miners' strike, compounded by the various industrial accidents (Abbeystead, Oxford Circus, the numerous railways accidents) and terrorist bombings (Heathrow, Brighton) and the long running investigations into police corruption. For some reason it seems to scream for a Promethean angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Japan, <i>A Monster with 21 Faces </i>could be the title, after the mysterious terrorists behind the <i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Monster_with_21_Faces\" target=\"_blank\">Glico Morinaga case </a> </i>which happens to be the most infamous unsolved crime in Japanese history, perfect for a cabal of magi to solve. The whole incident sounds like something out of a cyberpunk novel anyway.<br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind, our angle with the satanic panic dark era is that the Satanic ritual abuse never actually happened, it was a moral panic meant to hide the activities of the real satanists on wall street and in the mega churches. Basically making the greed is good part of the 80s much more sinister.<br /> <br /> The era is sort of meant to be a beast and inferno crossover.<br /> <br /> Have you seen the list of books on the panic I recommended?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 11-04-2017, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T07:35:13-08:00","id":1156045,"title":"","content":"Well, I figured in this case the child abuse would be at the hands of overzealous law enforcement, therapists and district attorneys (Heroes?) who effectively browbeat the kids into making accusations and convinced them that they'd been abused, screwing up the lives of everyone involved with the justification that they're doing heroic work against evil.<br /> <br /> (About 20 years ago, DC comics had an imprint called Paradox Press that put out a number of graphic novels, one of which, Green Candles, involved the problems with &quot;recovered&quot; memories and a case of ritual satanic abuse. Kind of surprised it was never made into a film the way A History of Violence and Road to Perdition were, as I thought it would've made for a pretty effective psychological mystery thriller.)<br /> <br /> I'm trying to work out some sort of Geist/Compact-level Hunter concept about ghosts and hauntings, inspired by the likes of Ghostbusters, A Nightmare on Elm Street, Christine, The Dead Zone, Poltergeist, Ghost Story, and maybe Evil Dead.<br /> <br /> Also, I keep wondering if there's something for Changing Breeds in this somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T08:21:11-08:00","id":1156059,"title":"","content":"Can we expand the 1920s-1930s as well to some other splats? Hunter is full of two-fisted tales for storytelling back in that era, and Changeling could easily focus on the rising subcultures of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T10:34:31-08:00","id":1156091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1156045#post1156045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I figured in this case the child abuse would be at the hands of overzealous law enforcement, therapists and district attorneys (Heroes?) who effectively browbeat the kids into making accusations and convinced them that they'd been abused, screwing up the lives of everyone involved with the justification that they're doing heroic work against evil.<br /> <br /> (About 20 years ago, DC comics had an imprint called Paradox Press that put out a number of graphic novels, one of which, Green Candles, involved the problems with &quot;recovered&quot; memories and a case of ritual satanic abuse. Kind of surprised it was never made into a film the way A History of Violence and Road to Perdition were, as I thought it would've made for a pretty effective psychological mystery thriller.)<br /> <br /> I'm trying to work out some sort of Geist/Compact-level Hunter concept about ghosts and hauntings, inspired by the likes of Ghostbusters, A Nightmare on Elm Street, Christine, The Dead Zone, Poltergeist, Ghost Story, and maybe Evil Dead.<br /> <br /> Also, I keep wondering if there's something for Changing Breeds in this somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is exactly what I was thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T15:15:20-08:00","id":1156170,"title":"","content":"<b>1984: The Haunted Valley</b>, (working title) set in the San Fernando Valley and it's LA commuter towns (the world you see in Fast Times at Ridgemont High, Valley Girl, ET, and The Karate Kid) and/or Orange Valley (Poltergeist), based around the idea that back in the 1920s, an architect built a building in LA designed to harness spiritual energy from the underworld, perhaps with the idea of summoning some ancient god. Because of certain astrological alignments, that building has become active and is causing a massive upswing in hauntings and other paranormal disturbances in the region. The PCs are from these surrounding small towns (ideally teens and 20somethings) forced to deal with things like their suburb being haunted by bodies that weren't moved from the graveyard the new neighborhood was built on, the ghost of a dead serial killer coming back for revenge on the children of the vigilante mob that killed him, weird government investigators and the like. This eventually leads them to the corrupt book of ancient lore used by the architect and his building. Maybe primarily for Geist and Hunter, and perhaps Second Sight. It may also fit with Mummy, but I'm not familiar enough with that game to say for sure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 11-05-2017, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T15:33:11-08:00","id":1156173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1156170#post1156170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>1984: The Haunted Valley</b>, (working title) set in the San Fernando Valley and it's LA commuter towns (the world you see in Fast Times at Ridgemont High, Valley Girl, ET, and The Karate Kid) and/or Orange Valley (Poltergeist), based around the idea that back in the 1920s, an architect built a building in LA designed to harness spiritual energy from the underworld, perhaps with the idea of summoning some ancient god. Because of certain astrological alignments, that building has become active and is causing a massive upswing in hauntings and other paranormal disturbances in the region. The PCs are from these surrounding small towns (ideally teens and 20somethings) forced to deal with things like their suburb being haunted by bodies that weren't moved from the graveyard the new neighborhood was built on, the ghost of a dead serial killer coming back for revenge on the children of the vigilante mob that killed him, weird government investigators and the like. This eventually leads them to the corrupt book of ancient lore used by the architect and his building. Maybe primarily for Geist and Hunter, and perhaps Second Sight. It may also fit with Mummy, but I'm not familiar enough with that game to say for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the architect could <i>be</i> a Tef-Aabhi mummy. As for why they designed it? Who knows - maybe even the mummy themselves forgot. Either way, it could trigger every Arisen in the area waking towards some purpose (to include Mummies, regardless of who the architect and their plan is).<br /> <br /> The whole thing also sounds like an Occult Matrix, if you wanted Demon or general God-Machine involvement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T14:18:11-08:00","id":1156474,"title":"","content":"(Very rough concept)<br /> <b>1984: Diamond Dogs</b>, taking it's name from David Bowie's 1974 album (which apparently started as an effort to turn Orwell's 1984 into a stage musical), set in London, among the youth culture of the Blitz Kids/New Romantics and the city's gay population, with the period's socio-economic upheavals and the beginnings of the AIDs crisis perpetually lurking around the edges of everything. I'm thinking this might be primarily a Changeling: The Lost setting, with possible Promethean and Vampire angles as add-ons, something with a lot of the overtones and themes you see in the world of people like Clive Barker, Neil Gaiman, Grant Morrison and the like. Themes of alienation from &quot;respectable&quot; mainstream society and wanting to make one's own mark on the world, with a lot of urban dark fantasy elements mixed in. <br /> <br /> And, as a possible title for a Japanese/Tokyo cyberpunk setting (probably focused on Mage), <b>1984: Burst City</b>, which is the name of this somewhat weird Japanese dystopian punk rock musical action movie from the early 80s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T14:39:40-08:00","id":1156482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flyboy254</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1144192-ideas-for-homebrewed-dark-eras?p=1156059#post1156059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we expand the 1920s-1930s as well to some other splats? Hunter is full of two-fisted tales for storytelling back in that era, and Changeling could easily focus on the rising subcultures of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Eras: Roaring 20s<ul><li>The Beautiful &amp; The Damned (Vampire in the vein of F. Scott Fitzgerald)</li> <li>The Lost Generation (Changeling in Paris among the expatriates)</li> <li>The Waste Land (Promethean in the after math of the Great War)</li> <li>Metropolis (Mage and maybe Demon in New York City working in the themes of the Fritz Lang film)</li> <li>Shadows Out of Time (Mummy and Hunter dealing with ancient eldritch horrors as envisioned by Lovecraft)</li> <li>Hard Liquor (Beast in the age of Prohibition)</li> </ul>And maybe something with Werewolf dealing with the rise of the KKK in the midwest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T11:25:43-08:00","id":1157795,"title":"","content":"I'm currently trying to work out some sort of concept revolving around Stephen King's early work, as well as that of other paperback horror material of the period (<i>1984: King Country</i> or something like that), primarily aimed at Hunters and the sort of characters from the core book, Second Sight and Innocents. Classmates that turn out to be mentally unstable psychokinetics or are possessed by haunted cars, buried ancient alien vessels, unfathomable horrors in the town sewer, cursed hotels, small towns that up and die for mysterious reasons, cursed burial grounds, werewolf murders, demonically possessed industrial machinery, corn gods, and people who wake up from comas with psychic powers. And lurking in the background are mysterious organizations (TFV, Cheiron, Vanguard, Barrett Commission, Null Mysteriis) that seem to want to harness or control these forces, especially any children who seem to develop special abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T18:05:40-08:00","id":1159649,"title":"","content":"This kind of overlaps with the Souless and the Damned timelinewise, but I thought Promethean during the height of the silk road trade (Pax Mongolia contemporary with Marco Polo's journeys for the most part.) would be cool. The silk road has so many themes appropriate for Promethean, after all the road itself is the ultimate road trip adventure, and the fact that its two endpoints (China and Europe/Middle East) also connect two disparate forms of alchemy seems far too appropriate. Would also be an opportunity to consider lineages that depart from the largely Western/Middle Eastern stories (with Ulgans being the primary exceptions.) for some new stuff. (I remember Tulpas were a concept that was only touched on in 1e, Tibet making up a large part of the road would be an opportunity to expand on that.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5823-ravian3","name":"Ravian3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}